  "scope": "Reuse order lemmas in Pell power recovery",
  "validation": "Paired target and three direct clients under the module directory pass with identical client objects; refreshed CarrierSoundness source/object receipt matches. Eighteen retained declaration type/axiom reports, 28,977 global simp and 13,172 instances match, with two private wrappers removed. Separate paired FirstNorm → rebuilt FirstIndex → adopted PowerRecovery replay passes with identical PowerRecovery output objects.",
  "limitations": [
    "The initial CarrierRadix client runs used an old CarrierSoundness and are superseded by fresh-provider replays; original receipts/logs are retained but archived compiled objects are excluded.",
    "The initial standalone final target output/log paths were reused. The author README/audit predates target adoption and describes FirstNorm as proposed; the post-commit peer review and separately recorded combined replay reflect the later adopted state.",
    "The combined replay does not rebuild PowerRecovery downstream clients. Its prior HalfIndex producer used pre-modular PellResidueClasses object 110e85d1… from source 5c70f7f7…; current source is a0a54a63…. Other project/Foundation/package dependencies remain cached and no complete current-source closure is claimed.",
    "Two removed private names were searched only in tracked Lean/Python code under the research area; untracked files, other types, dynamically constructed names and downstream consumers were not exhaustively searched.",
    "One paired shared-load timing sample is not a general benchmark. Probes do not cover every persistent environment extension. Compiled objects are excluded; their input/output hashes and commands are preserved in receipts."
  ],
